      "text": "Thy cheeks have been shown to be vessels of perfume in the world, O wise one, which draw forth life-creating drink for the faithful, O apostle Philip. For, possessed of works which led up to divine vision, thou didst become a follower and herald of Christ; with teachings thou didst adorn the barren and childless Church of the Gentiles for Him Who rejoiceth in the children therein. Pray thou that it be delivered from every want and evil circumstances, for thou art able to do much, drawing nigh unto Him.",
